# Line-ending policy: LF in the repository and LF on checkout, everywhere.
#
# This is load-bearing, not hygiene. Two things depend on it:
#
#   * Golden-file tests (section 2.11 onward) compare exact command output.
#     If expected-output files carry CRLF on Windows and LF in CI, every one
#     of them fails with a diff that is invisible on screen.
#   * Section 3.6 requires the Onboarding Brief to render byte-identically
#     across runs. That determinism is what section 6.10 later relies on to
#     prove the lite/cloud content-identity claim.
#
# Git for Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout by default, so this must be
# stated explicitly rather than assumed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must never be line-ending converted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.db   binary
*.pack binary
*.idx  binary
